figures.caption:
Graph depicting the χ ν 2 \chi^{2}_{
u} test values versus the coupling constant η o \eta_{o} across various NSI neutrino models. Continuous lines indicate the χ ν 2 \chi^{2}_{
u} values for distinct λ Z ′ / R ⊙ \lambda_{Z^{\prime}}/R_{\odot} values, with colour coding as follows: 0.05 (Turquoise), 0.1 (Tomato), 1 (Blue), 5 (Red), 10 (Gold), 50 (Green), 100 (Light Brown), and 1000 (Cyan). The vertical line corresponding to η o = 0 \eta_{o}=0 represents the standard model, while the horizontal line at χ ν 2 = 3.1 \chi^{2}_{
u}=3.1 indicates the quality of fit for the current data. The yellow circle represents the χ ν 2 \chi^{2}_{
u} of the current neutrino flavour oscillation model.

